yabasanshiro-fastforward.patch, ours (1.1.0): the auto frame skip comes back
on when fast forward ends.

retro_run turned YabaSanshiro's auto frame skip off while the frontend fast
forwards (its speed limiter would hold the game at 1x), but the test ran only
while fast forward was on, so it never turned the skip on again: after one
SELECT+R2 every frame was drawn until the next game. On a GKD Pixel 2
(1.1.0-rc.6, 2026-11-20) Virtua Fighter 2 went from 0.30x to 0.20x after five
seconds of fast forward, its frames all drawn (the skip's state read from the
core: off). Now the skip follows the answer to GET_FASTFORWARDING when it
changes, and only then, as EnableAutoFrameSkip restarts its clock: after the
same five seconds the skip is on again and the game back at 0.30x (rc.7).
git apply skips this preamble.

diff --color -ruN a/yabause/src/libretro/libretro.c c/yabause/src/libretro/libretro.c
--- a/yabause/src/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/yabause/src/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -1390,12 +1390,27 @@
          PERCore->Init();
    }
 
-   if (environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_FASTFORWARDING, &fastforward) && fastforward)
+   /* ZyperOS (yabasanshiro-fastforward.patch): the auto frame skip is off
+    * while the frontend fast-forwards (its speed limiter would hold the game
+    * at 1x) and on again when it stops. The test this replaced ran only
+    * while fast forward was on, so it turned the skip off and never back:
+    * after one fast forward every frame was drawn until the next game,
+    * Virtua Fighter 2 0.30x -> 0.20x on the GKD Pixel 2 (2026-11-20). Acted
+    * on at a change of the answer only: EnableAutoFrameSkip restarts its
+    * clock. */
    {
-      if (g_frame_skip == 1 && !fastforward)
-         EnableAutoFrameSkip();
-      else
-         DisableAutoFrameSkip();
+      static bool ff_was = false;
+
+      if (!environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_FASTFORWARDING, &fastforward))
+         fastforward = false;
+      if (fastforward != ff_was)
+      {
+         ff_was = fastforward;
+         if (fastforward)
+            DisableAutoFrameSkip();
+         else if (g_frame_skip == 1)
+            EnableAutoFrameSkip();
+      }
    }
 
    //YabauseExec(); runs from handle events
